@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Acceptable Use Policy (AUP) — SaveZonix";
}

<section class="legal-page">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
        <partial name="_LegalNav" model='(string)"AcceptableUse"' />

        <div class="legal-header">
            <h1 class="legal-title">Acceptable Use Policy (AUP)</h1>
            <div class="legal-meta">
                <span>Safe Computing Standards &bull; Prohibited Activities &bull; Compliance</span>
                <span>Last Updated: October 19, 2026</span>
                <span>Enforceable User Policy</span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-content">
            <div class="highlight-box">
                <strong>PURPOSE:</strong> This Acceptable Use Policy (AUP) defines the mandatory behavioral and operational standards governing the use of SaveZonix desktop applications, browser companion extensions, and local web tools. Violation of this policy constitutes a material breach of our Terms of Service and may result in immediate revocation of access and referral to legal authorities where appropriate.
            </div>

            <h2>1. Permitted Lawful Uses</h2>
            <p>SaveZonix is engineered to foster fair personal access, network protocol research, and authorized media archiving. Legitimate permitted activities include:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Downloading open-access educational lectures, university symposia, and research presentations.</li>
                <li>Preserving public domain video archives, historical government footage, and open-license media.</li>
                <li>Archiving personal live broadcasts, family home videos, or user-authored creative works.</li>
                <li>Conducting lawful fair-use preservation for commentary, critique, scholarship, or news reporting.</li>
                <li>Benchmarking network throughput, TCP connection pooling, and HLS/DASH chunked transport mechanics for educational and development purposes.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>2. Strictly Prohibited Activities</h2>
            <p>Under no circumstances may SaveZonix be used for:</p>
            <ul>
                <li><strong>Commercial Piracy &amp; Unauthorized Distribution:</strong> Downloading, selling, redistributing, or publicly broadcasting copyrighted commercial cinema, subscription television, pay-per-view events, or proprietary musical albums without written authorization from rights holders.</li>
                <li><strong>Circumvention of Technological Protection Measures (DRM):</strong> Attempting to tamper with, defeat, decrypt, or reverse-engineer hardware-level or software-level Digital Rights Management (DRM) technologies (including Google Widevine, Apple FairPlay, Microsoft PlayReady, or encrypted HDCP).</li>
                <li><strong>Abusive Scraping &amp; Infrastructure Degradation:</strong> Launching automated, distributed denial-of-service (DDoS) loops, high-frequency request floods, or malicious multi-threaded requests designed to degrade or crash third-party servers.</li>
                <li><strong>Harmful, Exploitative, or Unlawful Material:</strong> Processing, storing, or transmitting any child sexual abuse material (CSAM), non-consensual imagery, terrorist propaganda, hate speech, or content violating statutory criminal codes in any jurisdiction.</li>
                <li><strong>Third-Party Terms Violation:</strong> Engaging in activities designed to exploit or compromise the operational security of any streaming provider.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>3. Investigation, Enforcement &amp; Account Termination</h2>
            <p>SaveZonix reserves the absolute right to investigate any reported abuse, terminate access or account privileges of repeat violators, and cooperate fully with law enforcement authorities and copyright holders regarding any unlawful conduct.</p>

            <h2>4. Reporting Abuse</h2>
            <p>To report any abuse, unlawful activity, or policy violation involving SaveZonix, please contact our compliance desk immediately at <a href="mailto:savezonix@gmail.com" class="auth-link">savezonix@gmail.com</a>.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
